WEBVTT

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:34.110
Hey, want to go to Ikebukuro 
to hang out tomorrow?

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.210
Ikebukuro?

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:36.110
Yeah.

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.780
We can check out the planetarium, and...

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:39.740
Oh, I saw that by myself the other day.

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:41.140
We can have crêpes.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:43.160
I stood in line for an hour by myself for one.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.050
I want to check out the VR park.

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:46.620
I haven't been there.

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:50.910
I'm going to watch a movie with 
my parents tomorrow, though.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.060
Sorry.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.450
Okay.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:54.870
What about you, Aoi-chan?

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:58.030
I-I'll...

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:01.510
<i>What should I do if Hinata isn't going?</i>

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:04.910
You can't even go hang out without me?

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:06.930
You're so helpless.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:09.560
I'll go.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:11.470
Yay!

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:12.840
Great!

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:15.630
Okay, let's meet at Hanno 
Station tomorrow at ten.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:21.660
The crêpes in Ikebukuro were delicious.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:22.650
Yeah.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.160
The planetarium was pretty, too.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:26.650
Yeah.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:30.570
<i>Jeez, is she really going 
to be okay without me?</i>

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:33.920
<i>I hope she doesn't get left out because 
she can't keep up with the conversation.</i>

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.510
<i>I said I would in the heat of the moment...</i>

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:41.970
<i>But I think I might be a bit 
uneasy without Hinata there.</i>

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:44.970
So, like...

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:44.970
Say, Hinata...

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.430
Y-Yeah?

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.480
What were you saying?

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.910
Oh, nothing, really.

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:52.820
Okay.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:54.230
See you later, then.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:55.290
Okay.

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:56.280
Bye.

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:05.100
Oh, well...

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:10.580
<b>Season of Misunderstandings</b>

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:21.370
Morning.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:22.590
Morning.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:27.010
Where's Mom? Is she still sleeping?

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:29.020
She went to work a while ago.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:31.770
Isn't she coming to the movies?

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.270
It's Sunday that we're going to the movies.

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:37.660
You need to pay attention 
when people are talking.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.300
I have work in the afternoon, too.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:42.520
<i>It was tomorrow?</i>

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:44.780
<i>I could probably still catch up with Aoi and...</i>

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:48.120
<i>They must be on the train by now.</i>

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:49.840
<i>Besides...</i>

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:53.820
Really? You mixed up Saturday and Sunday?

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:55.890
You're such a ditz!

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:57.170
Pfft!

00:03:58.610 --> 00:03:59.520
Whatever.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.680
I already went to Ikebukuro the other day.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.930
<b>Kokona-chan
(Home)

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:13.490
Maybe she went out somewhere.

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:19.220
The weather's nice, after all.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:25.290
There!

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:27.700
Wow, amazing!

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:33.410
<i>Is Aoi really going to be okay without me?</i>

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:36.630
Oh, fine.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:39.290
I guess I'll send her a message.

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:42.510
Aoi sent you a photo.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:42.510
Aoi?

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:45.910
Hey, I guess she <i>is</i> freaking out without me.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:49.660
<i>We're headed to the planetarium.</i>

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:52.100
<i>Your movie must be starting about now.</i>

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:54.440
<i>Let me know what you think of it later.</i>

00:04:57.910 --> 00:04:59.570
What should I say?

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:02.780
Eh, I can deal with it later.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:05.410
I'm glad she's having fun.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:08.120
Hanno Shopping District

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.170
Hinata-chan!

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:19.380
Kaede-san, and...

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:22.420
Oh, I haven't introduced 
you to her yet, have I?

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:23.880
She's Yuka.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.340
You must be Hinata-chan.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:27.870
Kaede has told me a lot about you.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:31.300
I've heard about you from Aoi, too, Yuka-san.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:32.430
Nice to meet you.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:33.890
Nice to meet you, too.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:39.880
Your outfit today is cute, Kaede-san.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:41.150
I-Is it?

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:42.750
Are you going out somewhere?

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:43.720
No.

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:45.190
We just got back.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:46.240
From the library.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:48.250
To study.

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:50.170
<i>Kaede-san's eyes are dead.</i>

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:53.620
But it was packed, so we decided 
to go to Kaede's place instead.

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:54.370
Oh, yeah!

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:56.170
Want to come with us, Hinata-chan?

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:58.340
B-But wouldn't I get in 
the way of your studying?

00:05:58.340 --> 00:05:59.750
Not at all!

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:04.340
In fact, Yuka might go a bit 
easier on me if you're there.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.400
Go easier?

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:06.760
She's so strict!

00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:07.810
She's a monster!

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:10.060
She's a monster of a teacher!

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:10.510
Study!

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:12.220
What's that about monsters?

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:20.980
The planetarium was so pretty.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.530
I felt like we were floating in space.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:25.160
The VR was amazing, too.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:27.760
It was amazingly scary.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:30.360
It was like we were actually flying.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:33.180
I never knew you had a 
fear of heights, Aoi-chan.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:35.240
She was screaming her head off.

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:39.500
So... I actually had my eyes 
closed for most of it.

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:42.320
So you were just sitting there rocking?

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:45.690
No, that was scary enough, too.

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:46.960
Say what?

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.130
Don't laugh at me! Jeez.

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:50.940
Oh, the line's moving.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:52.650
What should I get?

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:53.870
She changed the subject.

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:58.860
We waited in line for half an 
hour and finally got crêpes.

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:02.760
I waited in line for a whole hour by <i>myself.</i>

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:07.000
I guess Aoi's grown up a little.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:10.220
Thanks for waiting, Hinata-chan.

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:12.540
We only had rice crackers.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:14.500
Rice crackers with coffee?

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:18.280
Hey, odd pairings can be 
surprisingly good, too, you know.

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:21.460
Kind of like you and Yuka-san, huh?

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:24.410
Odd pairings.

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:27.480
Seriously, why is that?

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.800
Odd pairings are okay, too.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:32.250
Just get to work. From 
where we left off yesterday.

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:33.100
Fine.

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:34.060
You mean "Yes, ma'am"!

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:35.270
Yes, ma'am.

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:38.810
You're like a teacher, Yuka-san.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:41.040
Y-Yeah?

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.310
Aoi-chan said the same thing, too.

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:46.430
Yuka wants to become a 
teacher when she grows up.

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:47.870
Hey, Kaede!

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:49.210
What's the matter?

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:50.820
It's not something you need to hide.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:55.010
I think Yuka's cut out to be a teacher, too.

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:57.580
She's aware of what's going 
on around her, unlike me.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:03.080
And she's teaching me right 
now, too, because she cares.

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:06.150
What are you studying for right now?

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:09.840
I decided to go to college.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:11.610
College?

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:14.680
What are you going to do at college?

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:19.610
I don't have anything specific in mind yet.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:23.710
But that's exactly why 
I want to go to college.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.170
<b>Glossary of World History</b>

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.170
<b>English Grammar</b>

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.170
<b>Magical Classical Literature</b>

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:29.120
If I can get into a good school, I'll have 
that many more options for my future, too.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:31.340
Your future...

00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:36.320
I want to make sure I don't regret 
it when I choose what I want to do.

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:40.580
And to make sure I can keep 
mountain climbing, too.

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:45.270
All right, that's enough chatter.

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:46.830
Let's start studying.

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:49.900
You can do anything you put 
your mind to, you know.

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:51.090
Fine.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.750
We're starting with math today.

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:55.270
Let's review the problems 
you couldn't do last time.

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:02.930
<i>An odd pairing, huh?</i>

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:08.180
<i>I hope Hinata likes this gift.</i>

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:10.180
Hey, look.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:13.280
Mt. Fuji!

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:15.740
I never knew you could see it from here.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:19.790
There's a station on the 
Ikebukuro line called Fujimidai.

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:21.550
Oh, yeah.

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:24.670
You climbed it during 
summer break, didn't you?

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:27.100
I only made it partway up.

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:29.780
It's amazing that you even 
thought to climb it at all.

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:31.040
Is it?

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:34.550
I want to make it to the peak next year.

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:37.740
So I'm trying to build up 
some stamina for that.

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:44.870
What's wrong, Kasumi-san?

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:47.310
You've brightened up, Aoi-chan.

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:51.020
You used to be indoorsy 
and shy a long time ago.

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:53.290
Is it because you started mountain climbing?

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:54.190
A long time ago?

00:09:56.450 --> 00:10:00.470
Don't you remember that we were in the 
same class during middle school?

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:04.280
Of course.

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:07.900
S-Sorry, which year were 
we in the same class?

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:09.210
All three.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:09.960
Seriously?

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.540
I-I don't know what to say...

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:20.810
You seemed really unapproachable back in 
middle school, but now you're easy to talk to.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.010
Don't forget me this time.

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:25.330
Please.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:28.140
I-I look forward to our friendship, too.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:29.770
I'm so sorry.

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:32.720
Kasumi-chan speaks her mind, 
but she's not a bad person.

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:34.010
Don't let it get to you.

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:35.640
Okay.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:47.190
Sorry to make you wait.

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:48.210
Let's go.

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:48.570
Okay.

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:49.070
Aoi...

00:10:49.070 --> 00:10:51.460
You know that crêpe you were eating...

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:53.200
That horned owl...

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:57.460
Actually, Hinata had a 
crêpe the other day, and...

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:05.470
Okay, I'm going this way.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.340
Okay, bye.

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:08.760
See you at school.

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:10.480
Don't forget about me again.

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.300
D-Don't worry.

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:14.060
Okay, bye.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:17.690
Why couldn't I say hi to her?

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.240
<b>How was the movie?</b>

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.240
<b>I bought you a gift from Ikebukuro.
Hope you like it</b>

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:29.050
A gift? Really?

00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:35.880
What's going on with me?

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:39.210
She had fun, right?

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:44.150
And yet...

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:59.940
<b>To Be Continued</b>
